1
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:40,960
You saved my mother, Thong?

2
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,280
I didn't save her.

3
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:45,000
And she wasn't your mother either.

4
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:48,240
Prajak took your mother away
long before that.

5
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:50,920
And he didn't even know
he had two daughters.

6
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,000
We look more alike
as we get older, don't we?

7
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,520
-Yes.
-<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Aunt Da has a twin?</font></font></i>

8
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:57,600
Yes.

9
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,360
You can't tell them apart.

10
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:03,800
And the woman who was just here?
Who was she?

11
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:06,520
Lada, your aunt.

12
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,320
Nada, your mother,

13
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,080
died a long time ago.

14
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:14,720
I'm planning to take Phakorn back
to Bangkok now. You should come with us.

15
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,000
You go ahead, Uncle.

16
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:19,600
I want to stay
and wait for news about Wee.

17
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If I'd died</font></font></i>

18
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">instead of Wee,</font></font></i>

19
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:28,240
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">everyone would be happier, wouldn't they?</font></font></i>

20
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:32,600
Nada, your mother, died a long time ago.

21
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:37,920
How did my mother die?

22
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,640
How did my mother die?

23
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,640
Thong, is the room ready?

24
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,000
-Yes, sir.
-Come on.

25
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,000
This way, sir.

26
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,360
Lada will let her out later.

27
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:02,400
You just guard the house
and make sure no one gets in.

28
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:49,280
How did I end up here?

29
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:00,360
Help! Help!

30
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,600
Is anyone out there? Help me!

31
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:12,000
Help!

32
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:14,560
Help!

33
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,480
Lada!

34
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,840
Lada! I'm in here!

35
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:25,920
Thamrong!

36
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,160
Lada!

37
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,720
I'm in here! I'm trapped!

38
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,200
Help me!

39
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,720
Help!

40
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,760
Uncle Thamrong knew everything all along.

41
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:42,160
Yes.

42
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,960
My mother was locked up until she died?

43
00:07:58,880 --> 00:07:59,960
Yes.

44
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,960
Your mother died locked in that room.

45
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,360
What did you do to my mother, Thong?

46
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:16,720
Did you kill her?

47
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:17,880
No.

48
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:19,880
I didn't.

49
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:22,280
Was it Ms. Lada?

50
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,040
No.

51
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:31,080
Not long after we locked Ms. Nada
in that room,

52
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:34,799
I heard that Mr. Rawich had been shot dead

53
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:37,400
and Ms. Lada was seriously injured.

54
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,760
The island was swarming with police.

55
00:08:40,799 --> 00:08:42,600
I was afraid they'd arrest me,

56
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:46,280
so I ran away,
leaving Ms. Nada locked inside.

57
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,160
Once things quieted down, I rushed back.

58
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,200
But it was too late.

59
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:41,400
So I asked some friends
to arrange for Ms. Nada to be cremated

60
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:44,080
alongside unclaimed bodies
during a mass cremation ceremony.

61
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,640
Then I secretly took her ashes
to the temple

62
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:51,080
to make amends for what I'd done.

63
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,840
I've seen my mother's ashes at the temple.

64
00:09:58,080 --> 00:10:00,160
Were you the one
who left the garland for her?

65
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:04,200
NADA TAYAWAT - TAWAN ISLAND TEMPLE

66
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,280
It was probably Ms. Lada.

67
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,040
Why didn't Uncle Thamrong
come back to save my mother?

68
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,880
Ms. Lada was seriously injured.

69
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,440
Mr. Thamrong loved her so much

70
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:48,800
that nothing else mattered to him anymore.

71
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,080
He must've felt guilty.

72
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:59,440
That's why he's helped my family
all these years.

73
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,880
I've told you everything.

74
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,840
Can I go now?

75
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,720
DAENG BOATMAN

76
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:40,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Hello, Thong. Need the boat today?</font></font></i>

77
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,480
I'm not Thong.

78
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:45,640
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Oh.</font></font></i>

79
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,760
Excuse me, sir.

80
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:50,440
You take passengers
to and from the island, right?

81
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,400
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Yes.</font></font></i>

82
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:55,360
I need a boat back to the mainland.

83
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:13,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">How long have you known</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">about Ms. Nada, Uncle?</font></font></i>

84
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,720
Since shortly before Ms. Nada got married.

85
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:22,880
Even back then, I noticed

86
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:26,640
she sometimes acted strangely.
She wasn't like herself at all.

87
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:31,440
Others might not have noticed,
but I could tell something was off.

88
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:54,560
-Are you full already?
-Not yet.

89
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:57,480
I'll be back to finish eating.
I just need to use the restroom.

90
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:58,560
Okay.

91
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:05,240
Thank you.

92
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:26,760
How did it go? Did Mr. Rawich notice?

93
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:29,320
He had no idea.

94
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:35,920
See? I told you we look exactly alike.

95
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:40,240
Whenever you don't feel like
going to events with your family,

96
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,880
just give me a call.

97
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:45,120
I love dressing up
and being around people.

98
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,320
Sure.

99
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,240
Well…

100
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,320
I'd better go
before Mr. Rawich gets suspicious.

101
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:54,040
I told him I was going to the restroom.

102
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,800
Okay.

103
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,280
I'll call you.

104
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:20,800
Mr. Thamrong.

105
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,240
You're not Ms. Nada. Who are you?

106
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,600
If I'm not Nada, then who am I?

107
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:31,440
Let go of me, or I'll tell Mr. Nimit.

108
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,480
Before you tell anyone,

109
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:36,320
why don't we go inside
and see Ms. Nada first?

110
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:45,680
Fine. I'll admit it.

111
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,160
Who are you?

112
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:58,320
Then why don't we

113
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:02,320
find somewhere else to talk?

114
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:09,720
Ms. Lada told me
how deeply she resented Prajak

115
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:12,200
for what he'd done to her family.

116
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:15,920
But I'd rather not go into that.

117
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,560
I don't know how much of it was true.

118
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:24,360
And you believed her?

119
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:28,360
Yes.

120
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:49,760
You don't see me
as just a substitute for Nada, do you?

121
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:56,120
I don't have feelings for Nada.

122
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:10,960
She's getting married,
and I don't have anyone.

123
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:16,040
Could you back me up?

124
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:19,640
How?

125
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:28,240
I want revenge on that bastard Prajak.

126
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,840
Please don't stand in my way.

127
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,280
Can you keep it a secret
that Nada and I are twins,

128
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:39,640
just like our relationship?

129
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,640
We've been together ever since.

130
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:50,600
Even if she's been using me,
I'm okay with it.

131
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:55,000
Because I've fallen in love with her.

132
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,680
Does my father know about this?

133
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:05,599
Mr. Nimit doesn't know.

134
00:17:08,319 --> 00:17:10,920
But you should've stopped her.

135
00:17:12,319 --> 00:17:15,240
Mr. Rawich and Ms. Nada
didn't deserve to die.

136
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,400
Alyssa.

137
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:21,640
I didn't know
every detail of her revenge plan.

138
00:17:23,359 --> 00:17:27,119
I only knew
what Ms. Lada allowed me to know.

139
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,200
And what about Ms. Pimpa?

140
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:39,920
I never meant for that to happen.

141
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:48,120
Did Aunt Da tell you to do it?

142
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,000
Don't worry, Ms. Alyssa.

143
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,520
I'll turn myself in. I promise.

144
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:06,200
I'm not worried.

145
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,760
I just want to know

146
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,720
what Ms. Lada plans to do next.

147
00:18:17,720 --> 00:18:19,480
Well, I think

148
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,920
we should pray

149
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,800
for Rawee's safety first.

150
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:58,480
Please be okay, Wee.

151
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:35,080
TAWAN ISLAND TOURIST BOAT SCHEDULE

152
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:41,120
Kong!

153
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,200
It's me.

154
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:50,320
I thought you were dead, man.

155
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,280
How did you know I was here?

156
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,800
I was told to follow Ms. Nada here.

157
00:19:58,520 --> 00:20:01,320
By who? Mr. Panas?

158
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:10,360
You were behind the last attack
on Ms. Nada, weren't you?

159
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:16,520
And now he's sent you to kill her again?

160
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:21,320
Yeah.

161
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,840
But I was worried about you,
so I looked for you first.

162
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:26,240
I knew you were still alive.

163
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:31,760
Wee, who did this to you?

164
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:36,360
What happened?

165
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:42,040
I…

166
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:45,480
I'm not ready to talk about it.

167
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:48,760
Alright.

168
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,280
You don't have to talk about it yet.

169
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:54,600
And your brother Korn was the first
to pack up and go back to Bangkok.

170
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:56,520
I thought he'd stay and help find you.

171
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:02,240
So what are you going to do now?
Everyone thinks you're dead.

172
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:08,440
Huh?

173
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:16,880
PHAKORN

174
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,080
What's gotten into you?

175
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,440
We've come this far.

176
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:16,720
We have nothing left to hide
from each other.

177
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:21,600
What's with the drama?

178
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:26,680
I feel like you and Uncle Thamrong
have been using me.

179
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,120
Tell me who you really are.

180
00:23:38,680 --> 00:23:39,840
Nada speaking.

181
00:23:42,040 --> 00:23:43,080
He's awake?

182
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,080
I'll be right there.

183
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:47,360
Grandfather's awake?

184
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:51,880
Yes. And don't you dare tell anyone.

185
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:12,880
Thank you so much, Dr. Tee,
for taking such good care of Father.

186
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,480
My pleasure.

187
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:18,360
He's always been in good health.

188
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:22,280
Could I ask you

189
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:25,520
to keep it a secret
that Father's regained consciousness?

190
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:31,280
I'm worried about his safety.

191
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,320
Please don't tell anyone he's awake yet.

192
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:39,480
Once I'm sure he's safe,

193
00:24:40,160 --> 00:24:41,840
I'll let everyone know myself.

194
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:44,920
Of course.

195
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:48,400
Thank you.

196
00:25:25,120 --> 00:25:26,760
You're awake, Father?

197
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:31,080
Phakorn.

198
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:34,240
Yes?

199
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:37,560
Phakorn isn't your son.

200
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:43,160
You've only just woken up.

201
00:25:43,240 --> 00:25:45,280
Let's not talk
about anything stressful yet.

202
00:25:47,680 --> 00:25:49,720
Rawee isn't your son either.

203
00:25:51,560 --> 00:25:53,480
Who are those two, really?

204
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:58,280
Why did you pass them off as your sons

205
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:01,520
and bring them into my family?

206
00:26:05,040 --> 00:26:07,640
No wonder you've been asleep for so long.

207
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:10,040
You woke up looking for a fight.

208
00:26:11,040 --> 00:26:14,200
I was going to let you rest comfortably
for a few more days.

209
00:26:14,280 --> 00:26:16,520
Don't bother questioning those two.

210
00:26:17,680 --> 00:26:19,800
If there's anyone
you should be suspicious of,

211
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:22,120
it's me.

212
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:26,680
What do you mean?

213
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:41,680
My name is Da.

214
00:26:42,480 --> 00:26:45,760
Short for Lada, not Nada.

215
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:50,800
You had no idea

216
00:26:51,520 --> 00:26:53,800
you had twin daughters, did you?

217
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:56,520
You always thought

218
00:26:57,120 --> 00:27:00,160
Nada was Nuan's only child, didn't you?

219
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:05,560
Guess

220
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:08,840
which one is Nada and which one is Lada.

221
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:20,320
What do you want?

222
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:23,560
Revenge on you.

223
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:27,880
What did I ever do to you?

224
00:27:29,080 --> 00:27:30,880
You still have to ask?

225
00:27:31,920 --> 00:27:34,920
After everything you've done?
Do you really have no idea?

226
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:39,280
You burned down our house.

227
00:27:41,280 --> 00:27:42,920
You caused Mother's death.

228
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:48,440
You took my little sister away from me.

229
00:27:51,120 --> 00:27:52,120
Do you have any idea

230
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:54,480
what I've been through

231
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:56,920
because of you?

232
00:28:14,480 --> 00:28:16,880
Dad! Why are you in here?

233
00:28:19,280 --> 00:28:21,040
Dad! What are you doing?

234
00:28:28,200 --> 00:28:29,200
Dad!

235
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:33,400
Dad! What are you doing?

236
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:36,960
-Don't! What are you doing?
-Let me go! Thong!

237
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:39,680
Da, get out of here.

238
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:42,080
-Where do you think you're going?
-Dad!

239
00:28:42,160 --> 00:28:44,080
-Let me go!
-Don't!

240
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:46,960
-Thong!
-Dad!

241
00:28:48,720 --> 00:28:51,520
Don't you remember
what that bastard Prajak did to us?

242
00:28:52,280 --> 00:28:54,080
Your face is like that because of him.

243
00:28:55,480 --> 00:28:57,880
She's his daughter, not mine.

244
00:28:58,480 --> 00:28:59,880
I'm gonna make her my wife.

245
00:29:00,640 --> 00:29:03,640
No, Dad! Don't!

246
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:05,280
Thong!

247
00:29:05,360 --> 00:29:06,600
Dad! Don't!

248
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:09,560
Dad!

249
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:23,000
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I had to live in constant fear.</font></font></i>

250
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:25,720
And it was all because of you.

251
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:28,040
I had such terrible nightmares

252
00:29:28,560 --> 00:29:30,520
that I could barely bring myself to sleep.

253
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:32,920
Do you have any idea how much I suffered

254
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:35,400
before I finally got through it?

255
00:29:37,280 --> 00:29:39,320
And you still have the nerve to ask?

256
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:42,600
You used your money and power

257
00:29:43,200 --> 00:29:44,920
to cover everything up,

258
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:47,000
leaving others to live with the trauma.

259
00:29:48,680 --> 00:29:50,200
I'm sorry, my child.

260
00:29:51,320 --> 00:29:52,880
You're not my fucking father!

261
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:56,680
And you never even wanted to be!
I never saw you as one!

262
00:29:57,800 --> 00:29:59,320
Want to hear more?

263
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:03,720
After all that misery,
something good finally happened.

264
00:30:05,280 --> 00:30:06,960
Thong managed
to sell some land he'd inherited.

265
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,400
He got a large sum of money

266
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:11,880
and sent me abroad to study,

267
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:14,640
hoping I'd forget everything terrible
that had happened.

268
00:30:16,640 --> 00:30:18,880
Nada had nothing to do with this.

269
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:21,360
How could she not?

270
00:30:24,760 --> 00:30:28,280
She abandoned me.
She lived a comfortable life.

271
00:30:30,360 --> 00:30:32,880
She never even bothered to look for me.

272
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:34,560
And don't give me that bullshit.

273
00:30:34,640 --> 00:30:37,720
She's the same age as me. She's my twin.

274
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:41,200
If I remembered her,
how could she not remember me?

275
00:30:41,280 --> 00:30:42,720
She got to live as a rich man's daughter.

276
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:46,440
And what about me?
Where did that leave me?

277
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:52,680
Thank you for taking such good care
of the house, Mr. Thamrong.

278
00:30:52,760 --> 00:30:53,720
You're welcome.

279
00:30:54,320 --> 00:30:57,240
You must really like it here, Ms. Nada.
You even bought a house.

280
00:30:58,040 --> 00:31:00,280
I love the atmosphere on Tawan Island.

281
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:03,320
You could always stay
at Mr. Nimit's resort when you visit.

282
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:06,520
But your boss wouldn't charge me.

283
00:31:07,840 --> 00:31:10,280
If Mr. Rawich's negotiations work out

284
00:31:10,360 --> 00:31:12,400
and he gets to open a resort here,

285
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:14,680
I might end up living here permanently.

286
00:31:15,200 --> 00:31:18,280
Then we'd definitely be competing
with your boss.

287
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:21,760
-I see.
-Thank you.

288
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:24,080
-My pleasure.
-I'd better change. Mr. Rawich's waiting.

289
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:25,080
Of course.

290
00:31:43,320 --> 00:31:44,280
Lada!

291
00:31:48,080 --> 00:31:49,480
What brings you here?

292
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:52,560
I missed you, of course.

293
00:31:55,400 --> 00:31:58,400
You've invited me so many times.
I finally got the chance to come.

294
00:32:01,280 --> 00:32:03,320
Your house is lovely.

295
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:06,840
Thank you.

296
00:32:09,880 --> 00:32:12,720
Have some orange juice. It's refreshing.

297
00:32:38,240 --> 00:32:39,960
Thong, is the room ready?

298
00:32:40,040 --> 00:32:41,040
-Yes, sir.
-Come on.

299
00:32:41,120 --> 00:32:42,160
This way, sir.

300
00:33:06,640 --> 00:33:07,800
Why are you stopping?

301
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:10,600
Is something wrong with the car?

302
00:33:12,040 --> 00:33:13,120
Just a moment.

303
00:33:30,160 --> 00:33:31,680
Is something wrong with the car?

304
00:33:33,920 --> 00:33:35,120
Nothing's wrong.

305
00:33:36,520 --> 00:33:37,840
Then why did you stop?

306
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:41,400
I've got a proposition for you.

307
00:33:43,280 --> 00:33:44,600
What proposition?

308
00:33:46,560 --> 00:33:48,840
You were Mr. Prajak Tayawat's secretary,
weren't you?

309
00:33:51,640 --> 00:33:52,800
I used to be.

310
00:33:54,320 --> 00:33:55,480
I've left the company now.

311
00:33:57,160 --> 00:34:00,280
He fired you for falling in love
with the chairman's daughter, right?

312
00:34:03,280 --> 00:34:04,560
If you already know, why ask?

313
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:08,920
Hey. Just tell me what you want.

314
00:34:09,679 --> 00:34:11,480
I want information on your former boss.

315
00:34:12,920 --> 00:34:14,199
What information?

316
00:34:15,199 --> 00:34:17,719
You know he's not an honest businessman.

317
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:20,760
He's always putting on an act.

318
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:23,560
He's clever. He knows
how to cover up his dirty deeds.

319
00:34:23,639 --> 00:34:26,360
I know you know all his secrets.

320
00:34:26,880 --> 00:34:28,840
Let's team up and expose him.

321
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:33,960
Whatever kind of man he is,

322
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:36,560
he's still my wife's father.

323
00:34:37,880 --> 00:34:41,199
Come on. You talk as if
he's accepted you as his son-in-law.

324
00:34:42,639 --> 00:34:44,040
Let's get back at him together.

325
00:34:45,040 --> 00:34:46,719
Your wife and child will live comfortably.

326
00:34:52,080 --> 00:34:54,560
Why should I trust you? Huh?

327
00:34:57,960 --> 00:35:00,120
I don't hold any grudges
against Mr. Prajak.

328
00:35:02,960 --> 00:35:04,560
I understand the situation.

329
00:35:05,720 --> 00:35:07,440
But I really can't help you.

330
00:35:10,200 --> 00:35:11,800
Just take me back to the resort.

331
00:35:12,400 --> 00:35:13,960
We're already way behind schedule.

332
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:20,480
So you won't listen to reason?

333
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:24,800
I know who you left your child
with and where.

334
00:35:24,880 --> 00:35:28,480
If you don't cooperate,
you'll never see your child again!

335
00:35:29,240 --> 00:35:30,240
Don't shoot, Thong!

336
00:35:43,680 --> 00:35:45,800
I told you not to shoot!

337
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,920
If I hadn't shot him, he'd have shot me!

338
00:35:53,560 --> 00:35:55,240
The police will be here soon.

339
00:35:58,400 --> 00:36:01,760
We'll have to change the plan.

340
00:36:19,600 --> 00:36:23,320
Da! Da!

341
00:36:24,080 --> 00:36:25,320
Da!

342
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,880
Rawich? Where's Rawich?

343
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:29,720
Let's get her to the hospital first.

344
00:36:37,120 --> 00:36:38,640
What about Nada's son?

345
00:36:39,360 --> 00:36:40,520
Rawee, of course.

346
00:36:41,560 --> 00:36:43,720
Rawee is your biological grandson.

347
00:36:45,880 --> 00:36:48,080
He survived because Thamrong

348
00:36:49,200 --> 00:36:51,760
called the person
who was looking after the baby.

349
00:36:53,400 --> 00:36:56,880
KIAT 078735063

350
00:37:05,360 --> 00:37:07,600
Kiat, take my son and run!

351
00:37:17,520 --> 00:37:18,920
Then where's Nada?

352
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:21,120
Nada

353
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:24,080
is standing right here, Father.

354
00:37:31,400 --> 00:37:33,640
Dad, I'd like to stay here
a little longer.

355
00:37:35,400 --> 00:37:37,400
I want to wait
for updates on the search for Wee.

356
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:40,480
I know you feel very guilty about Rawee.

357
00:37:42,080 --> 00:37:44,680
But it's your Uncle Jak's funeral.

358
00:37:45,760 --> 00:37:46,960
You really should come.

359
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:49,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">No matter how badly he treated you,</font></font></i>

360
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:52,400
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">he's gone now.</font></font></i>

361
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:55,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I want you to forgive him.</font></font></i>

362
00:37:57,760 --> 00:37:59,800
Please come back for Uncle Jak's funeral.

363
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:02,160
Do it for me, okay?

364
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:07,080
Okay, Dad.

365
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:11,000
I believe Rawee is a good man.

366
00:38:11,080 --> 00:38:14,000
I'm sure a higher power
is watching over him.

367
00:38:25,040 --> 00:38:26,760
Did Alyssa agree to come back?

368
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:29,160
Yes, she promised.

369
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:34,600
Alyssa seems especially concerned
about that Rawee.

370
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:37,640
My daughter has good taste.

371
00:38:38,760 --> 00:38:42,000
But I'm secretly rooting
for the younger brother.

372
00:38:42,080 --> 00:38:45,120
He's handsome, cool, kind,

373
00:38:45,200 --> 00:38:47,240
and has a bright future ahead of him.

374
00:38:50,040 --> 00:38:52,040
In the end, it's up to Alyssa.

375
00:39:32,640 --> 00:39:34,560
My place is a bit cramped.

376
00:39:35,160 --> 00:39:37,440
I just need a roof over my head.

377
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:43,640
If you want my help,
can you tell me something?

378
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:47,520
At least tell me
who can't know you're alive.

379
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:53,200
I'm the real grandson.

380
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:54,960
Ms. Nada's son.

381
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:13,480
GRANTOR: MR. PRAJAK TAYAWAT, CHAIRMAN

382
00:40:22,840 --> 00:40:24,320
What do you want?

383
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:27,320
I'll make it all up to you.

384
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:31,440
Transfer all the company's shares to me.

385
00:40:49,040 --> 00:40:50,680
TAYAWAT GROUP

386
00:40:50,760 --> 00:40:51,920
Hello.

387
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:06,040
I'm sorry for your loss, Alyssa.

388
00:41:08,440 --> 00:41:09,480
Thank you.

389
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:12,520
Mr. Nimit is inside. This way, please.

390
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:19,400
Mr. Thamrong!

391
00:41:20,120 --> 00:41:21,400
Have you heard anything about Rawee?

392
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:23,880
There's been no progress so far.

393
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:27,400
And I've just been informed

394
00:41:29,200 --> 00:41:30,880
that the search has been called off.

395
00:41:40,120 --> 00:41:41,440
Does that mean…

396
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:45,400
there's no hope left?

397
00:41:54,280 --> 00:41:55,120
-Mrs. Walai.
-Aunt Walai!

398
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:57,280
-Walai!
-Let's get her inside.

399
00:41:57,360 --> 00:41:58,440
Okay.

400
00:42:28,400 --> 00:42:29,520
Make sure you find it.

401
00:42:30,080 --> 00:42:31,760
I remember where it is.

402
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:06,200
Why isn't the door locked?

403
00:43:26,840 --> 00:43:27,760
Hello, Alyssa.

404
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:32,200
Where are you?
Do you know your mother fainted?

405
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:35,120
I called you from her phone,
but you didn't answer.

406
00:43:36,920 --> 00:43:39,760
How is she now? Which hospital are you at?

407
00:43:41,080 --> 00:43:43,120
The doctor wants to keep her overnight.

408
00:43:43,720 --> 00:43:47,160
If it weren't for my mother,
would you even talk to me?

409
00:43:49,680 --> 00:43:51,960
The person you should be
most worried about right now

410
00:43:52,040 --> 00:43:53,520
is your real mother.

411
00:45:19,120 --> 00:45:20,280
Who's there?

412
00:45:29,040 --> 00:45:30,040
Wee?

413
00:46:31,000 --> 00:46:34,520
I'M SORRY, BROTHER

414
00:46:43,880 --> 00:46:45,640
-Wee.
-Huh?

415
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:50,480
When we grow up, will we fight
like the brothers in this comic?

416
00:46:50,560 --> 00:46:52,720
You know, brothers killing each other?

417
00:47:00,240 --> 00:47:03,480
Are you crazy?
We've never even punched each other.

418
00:47:04,400 --> 00:47:06,600
That's because
you always let me have my way.

419
00:47:09,560 --> 00:47:11,920
I used to feel like I was all alone.

420
00:47:12,680 --> 00:47:13,600
Do you know

421
00:47:14,200 --> 00:47:16,160
how lucky I am to have Dad, Mom,

422
00:47:16,240 --> 00:47:17,400
and a brother like you?

423
00:47:18,600 --> 00:47:20,440
Why would I want to compete with you?

424
00:47:21,720 --> 00:47:22,800
I'm afraid you'd stop loving me.

425
00:47:25,800 --> 00:47:28,200
Stop thinking of yourself as adopted.

426
00:47:28,280 --> 00:47:30,240
Everyone else
has forgotten about it already.

427
00:47:33,200 --> 00:47:35,880
Comics are just made-up stories.

428
00:47:38,040 --> 00:47:40,200
Nothing like that will ever happen to us.

429
00:47:40,920 --> 00:47:42,680
We love each other so much.

430
00:47:43,600 --> 00:47:45,000
Now go to sleep.

431
00:47:50,160 --> 00:47:52,320
Hey, Wee!

432
00:47:52,400 --> 00:47:53,280
Yeah?

433
00:47:54,520 --> 00:47:55,960
Aren't you forgetting something?

434
00:48:00,080 --> 00:48:01,040
Good night.

435
00:48:02,200 --> 00:48:03,160
Go on.

436
00:48:58,120 --> 00:49:02,040
I've changed my mind. I'll pick Mom up.
I'll be there in ten minutes.

437
00:49:39,880 --> 00:49:43,160
Wee, how did it go? Did Korn see you?

438
00:49:43,240 --> 00:49:44,520
I hid just in time.

439
00:49:45,120 --> 00:49:48,280
I was so worried. Did you get it?

440
00:49:50,240 --> 00:49:51,400
Yeah.

441
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:01,000
Thank you.

442
00:50:12,640 --> 00:50:14,000
Korn is on his way.

443
00:50:14,080 --> 00:50:15,600
Okay.

444
00:50:16,240 --> 00:50:19,720
You can head home now.
Somphit is here to keep me company.

445
00:50:21,360 --> 00:50:23,000
Are you feeling better now?

446
00:50:30,480 --> 00:50:32,600
Physically, yes.

447
00:50:34,040 --> 00:50:35,720
But emotionally,

448
00:50:36,640 --> 00:50:38,280
I'm still struggling.

449
00:50:59,560 --> 00:51:01,160
Thank you so much.

450
00:51:06,320 --> 00:51:09,320
I'm the one
who should be apologizing to you.

451
00:51:11,120 --> 00:51:14,040
Wee went to Tawan Island
because I asked him to help me.

452
00:51:18,760 --> 00:51:22,280
Don't blame yourself. It's not your fault.

453
00:51:23,080 --> 00:51:24,600
Please don't think that way.

454
00:51:28,640 --> 00:51:31,120
I've been nothing but trouble for him.

455
00:51:32,160 --> 00:51:34,440
He keeps getting into trouble
because of me.

456
00:51:37,280 --> 00:51:39,760
Wee doesn't see it that way.

457
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:49,160
But I suppose
there's no point saying that now.

458
00:51:54,160 --> 00:51:56,280
Please don't say that.

459
00:51:57,080 --> 00:51:58,400
Don't give up hope yet.

460
00:52:00,120 --> 00:52:03,440
Wee could be stranded
on some deserted island.

461
00:52:04,280 --> 00:52:06,520
He's probably trying to contact you.

462
00:52:11,960 --> 00:52:12,920
You're right.

463
00:52:17,480 --> 00:52:19,440
I hope so too.

464
00:53:01,480 --> 00:53:03,000
We haven't talked all day.

465
00:53:03,840 --> 00:53:06,040
I've been busy. I'm sorry.

466
00:53:08,240 --> 00:53:10,600
It's okay. I understand.

467
00:53:14,720 --> 00:53:16,200
Are you ready?

468
00:53:18,320 --> 00:53:19,440
Ready for what?

469
00:53:21,720 --> 00:53:23,960
To move abroad with me.

470
00:53:24,600 --> 00:53:27,120
I'll get everything wrapped up
as soon as possible.

471
00:53:29,800 --> 00:53:32,000
I want to finally start a new life.

472
00:54:04,600 --> 00:54:06,080
Sorry.

473
00:54:11,400 --> 00:54:13,240
Want to use this to hold them together?

474
00:54:13,840 --> 00:54:15,040
Oh.

475
00:54:22,160 --> 00:54:23,280
Thank you so much.

476
00:54:24,400 --> 00:54:26,960
Thank you for taking the time
to make the copies.

477
00:54:28,080 --> 00:54:31,160
No problem. Anyway, enjoy reading it.

478
00:54:44,400 --> 00:54:46,000
Have they found Wee yet?

479
00:54:47,320 --> 00:54:49,040
You seem awfully worried about Wee.

480
00:54:50,080 --> 00:54:51,800
Aren't you worried about him?

481
00:54:54,440 --> 00:54:57,040
Wee came here
because Dad and I wanted him to.

482
00:54:58,040 --> 00:55:00,040
I can't leave until they find him.

483
00:55:02,720 --> 00:55:04,920
Wee keeps getting hurt because of me.

484
00:55:06,040 --> 00:55:08,840
If anything else happens to him,
I'll never forgive myself.

485
00:55:36,240 --> 00:55:38,120
Aren't you even going to say hello?

486
00:55:40,600 --> 00:55:43,440
Congratulations. You're finally rid
of the thorn in your side.

487
00:55:44,880 --> 00:55:46,200
What's that supposed to mean?

488
00:55:47,240 --> 00:55:48,480
You know exactly what I mean.

489
00:55:50,360 --> 00:55:53,600
You think I had something to do
with Wee's death?

490
00:55:57,280 --> 00:56:00,320
Absolutely. You're the number one suspect.

491
00:56:01,640 --> 00:56:04,160
When are you going to stop
thinking the worst of me?

492
00:56:05,680 --> 00:56:07,600
I know everything now.

493
00:56:08,960 --> 00:56:10,200
Stop pretending.

494
00:56:12,080 --> 00:56:15,840
Just because I'm not Ms. Nada's real son,
do you really have to hate me so much?

495
00:56:17,520 --> 00:56:19,760
You still don't realize
what you've done wrong?

496
00:56:21,360 --> 00:56:24,160
Okay, Alyssa. I'm sorry I lied to you.

497
00:56:24,960 --> 00:56:25,920
But

498
00:56:26,440 --> 00:56:28,480
you won't tell anyone
about this yet, right?

499
00:56:30,800 --> 00:56:31,880
Why?

500
00:56:33,120 --> 00:56:35,400
Afraid I'll tell everyone?

501
00:56:37,360 --> 00:56:38,680
Don't worry.

502
00:56:39,560 --> 00:56:40,760
I'll definitely speak up

503
00:56:41,480 --> 00:56:42,920
when I get the chance.

504
00:56:45,440 --> 00:56:46,640
Why?

505
00:56:47,560 --> 00:56:50,040
Now that you know
I'm not the rightful heir,

506
00:56:50,640 --> 00:56:53,320
you think you've picked the wrong guy,
so you're dumping me?

507
00:57:01,800 --> 00:57:04,840
No wonder you're not real brothers.

508
00:57:05,480 --> 00:57:06,880
You're nothing alike.

509
00:57:10,120 --> 00:57:11,840
If you're planning to kill me,

510
00:57:12,520 --> 00:57:13,520
go ahead.

511
00:57:14,160 --> 00:57:15,360
I'm not afraid.

512
00:57:16,160 --> 00:57:18,280
But you'd better hurry.

513
00:57:18,880 --> 00:57:20,440
Because the moment I get proof

514
00:57:20,520 --> 00:57:23,160
that you were involved in someone's death,

515
00:57:24,240 --> 00:57:25,600
I'll make sure you go to jail.

516
00:57:41,160 --> 00:57:45,120
Wee, I'm serious.
If you want to get everything back,

517
00:57:45,200 --> 00:57:46,920
we can't do this on our own.

518
00:57:47,000 --> 00:57:48,640
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">We need to find someone to help us.</font></font></i>

519
00:57:48,720 --> 00:57:50,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Or we need to gather more evidence first.</font></font></i>

520
00:57:50,960 --> 00:57:51,880
What's going on?

521
00:57:53,160 --> 00:57:55,480
Are you Mr. Thamrong Wongphisit?

522
00:57:56,080 --> 00:57:58,160
-Yes, that's me.
-Please come in to give a statement.

523
00:58:01,120 --> 00:58:02,840
You've always been reasonable

524
00:58:02,920 --> 00:58:05,400
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">and good at handling problems.</font></font></i>

525
00:58:05,480 --> 00:58:08,200
